messages:
maria: Quick Helm values question — trying to conditionally wire container env from a Secret depending on values.environment == 'prod' OR when values.useExternalSecrets == true. If useExternalSecrets we want the chart to NOT render any valueFrom/secretKeyRef and let ExternalSecret populate the pod. Any tips on best pattern?

maria: current naive snippet (not working because it renders an empty name):
```yaml
env:
  - name: DB_PASSWORD
    valueFrom:
      secretKeyRef:
        name: {{ .Values.db.secretName }}
        key: password
```

maria: For non-prod we set db.secretName to "app-staging-db" and for prod we want to require it. But when useExternalSecrets=true we set db.secretName: "" and helm tries to render the resource and k8s fails.

alex: TL;DR: don’t render the env block at all when using external secrets. Rendering an empty name will produce invalid k8s. Use an if/else around the whole list item.

alex: Example I use:
```yaml
{{- if not .Values.useExternalSecrets }}
- name: DB_PASSWORD
  valueFrom:
    secretKeyRef:
      name: {{ tpl .Values.db.secretName . }}
      key: password
{{- end }}
```

alex: Also use tpl() so values that are templates (like "{{ .Release.Name }}-db") get rendered. For prod you can add required: `{{ required "db.secretName is required in prod" .Values.db.secretName }}` in a _helpers.tpl or pre-install check.

maria: oh good point about tpl and required. Didn’t think about the templated name case.

tanya: If you want to be extra safe you can lookup the Secret and only render if it exists, which avoids a failed rollout when someone forgets to create the ExternalSecret/Secret:
```yaml
{{- $name := tpl .Values.db.secretName . }}
{{- $s := lookup "v1" "Secret" .Release.Namespace $name }}
{{- if and (not .Values.useExternalSecrets) $s }}
- name: DB_PASSWORD
  valueFrom:
    secretKeyRef:
      name: {{ $name }}
      key: password
{{- end }}
```

tanya: Note lookup requires Helm v3 and RBAC to allow list/get on Secrets if run as a helm operator. Might be overkill for most charts.

jordan: FWIW we saw a similar failure last week where people set secretName: "" in values for external secret mode. We added a lint rule in our repo: if useExternalSecrets is true then db.secretName must be absent or null, not an empty string. Can add a chart schema rule too.

maria: Good idea. Is there a quick YAML schema snippet for that?

jordan: Yup — in values.schema.json: 
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "useExternalSecrets": { "type": "boolean" },
    "db": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "secretName": { "anyOf": [ { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }, { "type": "null" } ] }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

jordan: That enforces either a non-empty string or null; then add a repo-level pre-commit hook to check combinations.

maria: Thanks all — I’ll change the template to not emit env entries when useExternalSecrets=true and add the schema rule.

deploy-bot: CI: helm lint passed for chart/myapp (branch: feature/helm-extsecret) :white_check_mark:

maria: @jordan can you also quick-verify infra Terraform for ExternalSecrets CRD? I think recent TF upgrade changed namespace-scoped permissions.

jordan: sure, will check and ping infra if we need RBAC tweaks.

maria: awesome, will open a tiny PR with the template + schema. Thanks :raised_hands:
